 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for delivery.** Committed revisions are pushed to browsers over WebSocket connections the project runs itself, getting fast updates without tying the board to a realtime vendor, at the cost of connection-capacity and reconnect operations the project owns. Five-second HTTPS polling and a hosted realtime service were weighed and rejected. See `docs/decisions/delivery-transport.md`.
